        "id": "p12-q10-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "What is the gradient and what is its meaning in this context?\n\n(Hint: think of the volume of a prism formula)",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Gradient $4.25$; the cross-sectional area of the prism.",
          "worked": "$\\begin{aligned}\\text{gradient}&=\\frac{34-0}{8-0}\\\\\\text{gradient}&=4.25\\end{aligned}$\n\nFor a prism, $V=Ah$, so $\\dfrac{V}{h}=A$. The gradient is the cross-sectional area.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 26
